<title>USA: Continental files $400 mln debt shelf.</title>
<headline>Continental files $400 mln debt shelf.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Continental Airlines Inc filed a shelf offering of up to $400 million in debt securities Monday with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission.</p>
<p>The Houston-based air carrier said proceeds from the sale will be used for general corporate purposes, which may include repaying outstanding debt and financing capital expenditures.</p>
<p>No underwriters were named in the shelf offering.</p>
